  "id": "COMPOUND:27718 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Benzo[F]Quinoline is implicated in the activity of DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step pathway. The evidence suggests that Benzo[F]Quinoline directly targets ME-180, which in turn is a target of multiple entities, including (15S,17R,19S)-15-ethyl-17-methoxy-1,11-diazapentacyclo[9.6.2.02,7.08,18.015,19]nonadeca-2,4,6,8(18)-tetraene and Isohelenin, Inula sp. All of these entities ultimately target DNA polymerase iota. This indicates that Benzo[F]Quinoline may exert its effects through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the inhibition or modulation of DNA polymerase iota. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, albeit indirect, relationship between Benzo[F]Quinoline and DNA polymerase iota, likely mediated through the intermediaries listed. The mechanism appears to involve a pathway where Benzo[F]Quinoline influences a series of targets that ultimately interact with DNA polymerase iota, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
